Full chats: the events of task tskrDgeaXOwcnO in byre (read_task_events with task_id tskrDgeaXOwcnO).

## Summary

Performance audit of the requested main commit examined server request handling, browser data loading and histories, query execution/probes/redaction, media delivery, store/derived data, search and background scheduling. Selected one small fix with measured gains.

Before: calendar subscription feeds read and checked every event column.
Now: feeds request only the eight fields their calendar encoder uses, preserving event selection, permission checks and calendar contents.

One changed production line in internal/db/savedsearch.go. Expanded endpoint regression coverage for timed events, all-day dates, description and location, retaining existing filtering, links and token alias checks. Added BenchmarkSavedSearchFeed over the existing synthetic school.

Five alternating production query rounds after warm-up, with identical event IDs and calendar field values: ordinary parent, 658 events, median 78.543 → 33.501 ms; owner, 668 events, 37.360 → 15.342 ms. These compare query forms on the existing live server; the branch was not deployed for measurement. Local complete-feed medians across five repetitions: 13.119 → 5.711 ms, 8.20 → 4.97 MB/op, 83,862 → 55,399 allocations/op. Focused tests, go vet ./..., formatting and diff checks passed. Review completed with no findings.

Deliberately left Loop history pagination, which requires a coordinated query/interface change; the similar-documents tool's whole-index scans, which lack measured noticeable latency; and roughly 8 ms of synthetic-school background search exclusion work, which does not justify additional machinery. No schema or interface changes. Merged main automatically without conflicts and left the merge uncommitted for byre.

## Reviews

