Calendar subscription feeds no longer load every column of each matching group. The saved-search query that builds an .ics file now asks only for start, end, all_day, path, name, description, and location (id still comes back with every row). Those are the fields the feed writes into each event. The existing feed test now checks the picnic's times, description, location, link, and all-day dates, and a benchmark times the same feed over the large sample school.

No significant findings.
